1
00:00:03,052 --> 00:00:05,060
When Mila plucks the rubber band,

2
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:06,494
it shakes and it sings!

3
00:00:06,544 --> 00:00:08,303
Noah hears it across the lab…

4
00:00:08,353 --> 00:00:10,410
but how did the sound get to him?

5
00:00:11,249 --> 00:00:13,193
Noah makes a ruler vibrate, bzzz!

6
00:00:13,243 --> 00:00:16,093
And when Mila talks with her hand on her throat,

7
00:00:16,143 --> 00:00:17,060
that shakes too!

8
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:19,648
So everything that makes a sound vibrates.

9
00:00:20,432 --> 00:00:21,946
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:24,462 --> 00:00:24,998
Mini mode!

11
00:00:25,048 --> 00:00:27,460
The rubber band pushes the air next to it.

12
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:29,160
That air pushes the next bit,

13
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:30,450
which pushes the next…

14
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,728
and a wave of pushes crosses the room!

15
00:00:33,545 --> 00:00:36,046
But the air doesn't travel, it shakes in place.

16
00:00:36,096 --> 00:00:38,977
It's the push that moves forward, like a stadium wave,

17
00:00:39,027 --> 00:00:40,980
where everyone stays in their place!

18
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:44,522
In your ear, the wave makes the eardrum shake,

19
00:00:44,572 --> 00:00:45,247
a thin skin.

20
00:00:45,297 --> 00:00:47,968
Then three tiny bones pass it to the cochlea,

21
00:00:48,018 --> 00:00:50,194
which tells the brain, and you hear!

22
00:00:51,012 --> 00:00:53,427
But in space, there is no air to push,

23
00:00:53,477 --> 00:00:54,659
so no sound at all!

24
00:00:54,709 --> 00:00:56,735
Mila shouts, Noah hears nothing…

25
00:00:56,785 --> 00:00:58,082
except on the radio.

26
00:00:58,852 --> 00:01:01,670
And that's how sound travels to our ears.

27
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:05,743
Whatever makes a sound vibrates; the air passes the vibration along,

28
00:01:05,793 --> 00:01:07,170
bit by bit, to your eardrum.

29
00:01:08,468 --> 00:01:09,153
With an adult:

30
00:01:09,203 --> 00:01:12,669
make the end of a ruler vibrate where it sticks out over the table.

31
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:14,818
The shorter it is, the higher the pitch!

32
00:01:15,951 --> 00:01:17,836
And why does popcorn pop?

33
00:01:17,886 --> 00:01:19,434
The answer tomorrow.
